{"duration_api_ms":292918,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"eb25b754-fa7c-4472-b118-76d7f3977b47","total_cost_usd":0.7919077,"usage":{"input_tokens":14,"cache_creation_input_tokens":84861,"cache_read_input_tokens":271592,"output_tokens":42471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":20730},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":84861,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":20177,"cache_read_input_tokens":88078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5239},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":5525,"outputTokens":28,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0005665000000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":42471,"cacheReadInputTokens":271592,"cacheCreationInputTokens":84861,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7913412000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":20730,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":84861,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer\":\"sample_construction_auditor\",\"paper_id\":\"bicycle-infrastructure-paper\",\"run_status\":\"ok\",\"summary\":\"The paper has no assigned/treated panel, but it has a sample flow from search hits to unique articles to relevance codes to openings to projects, plus a FINN.no listing appendix. I traced both. The listing counts and shares in Table 8 are internally consistent: 266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579, and the shares recompute. The main problems are in the pilot and full-run article flow. (1) Figure 1 and Section 3.1.2 divide counts of openings by counts of articles and hits. (2) The pilot has two relevance definitions (5 versus 3 relevant articles). (3) A footnote contradicts Table 3 on how the Stord article was coded. (4) The stated exclusion of truncated-text articles is not applied to the pilot. (5) The full-run construction is undefined: rounds, overlap with the pilot, deduplication and truncation handling, and article versus story units. (6) Human 'unclear' coding is not reconciled with the LLM's categories. (7) The validation set was reused after prompt revision, and date validation covers only three articles. (8) Project denominators switch between 43 and 44. (9) The Table 9 first-match rule contradicts its own example and Figure 2 colours. (10) The treatment of the 2024 data gap in Figure 3 is unclear. Parser quality was respected: the structured table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, and the page text and images were used instead.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-001\",\"category\":\"denominator_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"Figure 1 and Section 3.1.2 report '2 of 70 search hits' and '2 of 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)' as concerning an opening that took place. The 2 is a count of distinct openings (projects), not articles or hits, so the numerator and denominator are in different units.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample / Figure 1\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 3.1.4 states that five articles were coded relevant and these correspond to two unique openings (four Homborsund, one Stod). Figure 1's last bar is labelled 'Distinct openings that took place' (2), but the caption and text express it as a share of 70 hits and of 34 articles. Under the pilot coder's initial coding, 5 of 34 articles (about 15 percent) concern those two openings. Under the validation recoding, 3 of 34 do. The 6 percent figure therefore mixes projects with articles. The abstract's 'only two actual openings' is correctly phrased in project units.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Figure 1 chart also inspected on page_004.png: bars 70, 34 (49% retained), 5 (15% retained), 2.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"2 of 34 unique articles concern an opening\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"The 2 counts distinct openings; the articles about them number five (or three after recoding).\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Report the final funnel stage in one consistent unit. Give the number of articles reporting an opening (and under which relevance rule), and separately the number of distinct openings. Revise the '6 percent' sentence and the Figure 1 caption accordingly.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-002\",\"category\":\"variable_construction_unclear\",\"finding_summary\":\"The pilot uses two different definitions of 'relevant'. Figure 1 and Section 3.1.4 count 5 relevant articles. The validation (Tables 3-4, abstract) recodes the two pre-opening Homborsund articles as not relevant and uses 3. The recoding is applied to the human labels after the fact, and the manuscript does not say how the LLM prompt's relevance rule treats pre-opening articles.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4 Manual coding of the pilot\",\"text_quote\":\"they are therefore coded as not relevant, leaving three relevant articles\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. In the validation (Section 4), they are therefore coded as not relevant, leaving three relevant articles.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Figure 1 ('Coded relevant' = 5, 15% retained) and the 3.1.4 coding result (five relevant, eight unclear, 21 not relevant) use the original rule. Table 3/4 give 3 relevant for the pilot coder. The 5-to-3 change is disclosed, but the rule (an article is relevant only if published after the opening) is introduced as a pilot lesson. Table 1 lists relevance as 'Opening of a new walking and cycling path', with no timing condition. The LLM prompt is not reproduced (Appendix B only points to a repository). The reader cannot tell whether the LLM's 'Relevant' in Table 4 and the 92 articles in Table 6 are defined on the 3-article rule, the 5-article rule, or something else.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"they are therefore coded as not relevant, leaving three relevant articles\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Whitespace/line-wrap tolerant quote.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4\",\"text_quote\":\"The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Pilot relevant count\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"5 in the funnel versus 3 in validation; the LLM's operative definition is not stated in the paper.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"State the operative relevance rule (including the pre-opening and planned-opening treatment) as used by the human coders and the LLM prompt. Show Figure 1 and Tables 3-4 under the same rule, or label each count with its rule.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-003\",\"category\":\"data_flow_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was 'coded as not relevant by both human coders'. Section 4.1 and Table 3 say the second coder coded the Stord article as relevant (the only human disagreement).\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The 44 projects include ... the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 3 shows pilot coder Not relevant / second coder Relevant = 1 article. Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord municipality / Vestland County pedestrian-crossing article. Table 4 shows the same article is the only pilot-coder vs LLM disagreement, with the LLM (majority) coding it relevant. Footnote 3 therefore misdescribes the second coder's coding. The Stord (Vestland) project is also distinct from the Stod (Steinkjer) opening. Its inclusion in the 44 projects is explained only through the LLM flag, which the footnote does not say.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6\",\"text_quote\":\"96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote 3 (marker digit attached to 'The'); the sentence about Stord continues on the following lines.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1\",\"text_quote\":\"The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County over a pedestrian crossing.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Stord coded not relevant by both human coders\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Table 3 (cell 1 in Pilot not relevant / Second coder relevant) and the 4.1 text show the second coder coded it relevant.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Correct footnote 3 to state who coded the Stord article as relevant (second coder and LLM) and that the pilot coder coded it not relevant. State that its inclusion in the 44 projects rests on the LLM flag.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-004\",\"category\":\"sample_restriction_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"Section 3.1.1 says duplicates and articles with missing or truncated text are excluded before analysis, but the pilot's 34 unique articles still include four articles with 0-23 words and two further very short ones. These are coded 'unclear' and then folded into 'not relevant' in the agreement tables.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.1 News article base\",\"text_quote\":\"as well as articles with missing or truncated text, are excluded\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"These duplicates, as well as articles with missing or truncated text, are excluded before the analysis.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 3.1.2 says that in four of the 34 unique articles 'the full text in the archive was missing, with only 0-23 words'. Section 3.1.4 says six of the eight 'unclear' articles had too little text, the four missing-text ones and two very short ones. These articles remain in the 34-article denominator of Tables 3-4, where unclear is set to not relevant (Table 3 note, footnote 1). 6 of the 31 'not relevant' pilot-coder cells are therefore articles that carry no codable content. Whether the same exclusion was applied to the 3,187 full-run articles is not stated.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.1-3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"the full text in the archive was missing, with only 0–23 words\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text (exclusion rule)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.1\",\"text_quote\":\"as well as articles with missing or truncated text, are excluded\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"This resulted in five relevant articles, eight unclear and 21 not relevant.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Truncated/missing text articles are excluded\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S2\",\"S1\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Four missing-text and two very short articles remain in the 34-article pilot and in the agreement tables.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Reconcile the exclusion rule with the pilot flow. Either report agreement excluding the six uncodable articles, or state that the rule applies only to the full run. Report how many truncated-text articles were dropped from the 3,187.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-005\",\"category\":\"data_flow_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The full-run data flow cannot be reconstructed. 'Rounds 1-4' are never defined. The pilot window (2 Sept-10 Oct 2026) lies inside the 'rounds 2-4' window (Oct 2025-Oct 2026), and the manuscript does not say whether the 34 pilot articles are inside the 3,187. Yet the 96 articles and 44 projects add pilot articles to the 92 and 43.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 5 says the LLM coded 3,187 articles 'from rounds 2-4, published between October 2025 and October 2026'. Table 7 draws on 'rounds 1-4'. The pilot was drawn between 2 September and 10 October 2026, which falls inside that window. The 44 projects are described as the 43 from Section 5 plus Stord, so Homborsund and Stod must already be among the 43 through rounds 2-4 articles, while the pilot articles about them are added separately. Round boundaries, search terms/dates per round, and any overlap or deduplication across rounds and with the pilot are not given, so it is unclear whether any article or project is counted twice. The conclusion and abstract report only 43 projects, while Section 6 uses 44.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6\",\"text_quote\":\"96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 9 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md\",\"page\":9,\"page_label\":\"9\",\"section\":\"5 Results\",\"text_quote\":\"published between October 2025 and October 2026 in 236 different outlets\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote spans a line break in the PDF text.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"96 = 92 + 4 pilot; 44 = 43 + Stord\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Arithmetic adds up, but the round definitions and the overlap of the pilot with rounds 2-4 are not specified.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Define each round (dates, search terms, retrieval date, whether duplicates across rounds were removed) and state whether the pilot articles are inside or outside the 3,187. Provide a single flow of articles and projects across rounds and the pilot.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-006\",\"category\":\"data_flow_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"It is unclear whether the 3,187 coded articles and the 92 relevant articles are deduplicated. Section 3.1.1 says duplicates are excluded, but the authors report that the automatic duplicate check missed a near-identical article, and Section 6.4 says coverage must still be counted after duplicates are removed. 'Articles' and 'distinct stories' also appear to be used interchangeably.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":6,\"page_label\":\"6\",\"section\":\"3.1.4 / 6.4\",\"text_quote\":\"the automatic duplicate check missed the near-identical online and print versions of one article (Fanaposten)\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The LLM coded 3,187 articles ... The result was 92 articles reporting an opening and 43 unique projects.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"In the pilot, 36 of 70 hits (about 51 percent) were duplicates, and the automatic deduplication still missed at least one near-duplicate. For the 3,187 articles, the number of retrieved hits, the number of duplicates removed and the deduplication method are not reported. Table 7 counts '16 projects covered by more than one distinct story', while Section 5 says most projects are covered by one or two articles and the 92 articles map to 43 projects (about 2.1 per project). Section 6.4 says 'Coverage should be counted at project level after duplicates are removed'. This suggests that duplicated versions may remain in the 92, so the article-level counts and outlets (50) are not clearly in a consistent unit.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 6 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_006.md\",\"page\":6,\"page_label\":\"6\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"the automatic duplicate check missed the near-identical online and print versions of one article (Fanaposten)\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e13eccc23f4c883050d15bcf\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote spans a line break.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 12 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_012.md\",\"page\":12,\"page_label\":\"12\",\"section\":\"6.4\",\"text_quote\":\"Coverage should be counted at project level after duplicates are removed.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-a6c6d31e7be45f25b775aa47\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 11 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_011.md\",\"page\":11,\"page_label\":\"11\",\"section\":\"Table 7 note\",\"text_quote\":\"covered by more than one distinct story\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-95b2618a59737e0b1725c4df\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 7 note, footnote letter 'a' precedes 'Projects'.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Duplicates excluded before analysis\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"No full-run deduplication counts; evidence suggests duplicates may remain.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Report, for the full run, hits retrieved, duplicates and truncated-text articles removed, and the method. State whether the 92 relevant articles are unique stories or include duplicate versions.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-007\",\"category\":\"data_flow_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The selection of the 70 pilot search hits is not documented. The text gives a date window and one search term, but not how the 70 were drawn from the archive, the total number of hits in the window, or whether they are consecutive, random or top-ranked.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample\",\"text_quote\":\"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026 was extracted\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026 was extracted to test our approach.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 3.1.1 reports preliminary counts of 530 to 13,800 hits over three years depending on the term. The pilot yield (3 relevant of 34, about 9 percent) is used to argue that keyword search is too noisy, and the abstract generalises from it. The 3,187-article full run yields 92/3,187 (about 2.9 percent). Without the sampling rule the pilot yield cannot be interpreted, and the sample's representativeness for the full run cannot be judged.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"State how the 70 hits were selected from the archive and how many hits the search returned in the window.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-008\",\"category\":\"variable_construction_unclear\",\"finding_summary\":\"Human three-way relevance coding (relevant/no/unclear) and LLM coding are not reconciled. Humans coded 8 of 34 pilot articles 'unclear', while the LLM full run reports only 2 'unclear' of 3,187. The paper does not say how LLM 'unclear' outputs, or three-run ties across three categories, enter the 2x2 majority-vote Table 4.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":8,\"page_label\":\"8\",\"section\":\"4.2 / Table 4 note\",\"text_quote\":\"the table uses the majority of the three runs.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The LLM coded each article three times, and the table uses the majority of the three runs.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 3.1.4: human coding yielded five relevant, eight unclear, 21 not relevant (8/34 = 24 percent unclear). Footnote 1 on page 7 sets human 'unclear' to not relevant. Table 6 (page 10) reports Unclear 2 among 3,187 LLM-coded articles. The manuscript does not state the LLM's categories in the pilot, how many pilot articles were 'unclear' for the LLM, how 'unclear' or split votes were mapped to 2x2, or whether truncated-text and planned-opening articles (which humans coded unclear) were coded relevant, not relevant or unclear by the LLM.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 8 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md\",\"page\":8,\"page_label\":\"8\",\"section\":\"Table 4 note\",\"text_quote\":\"the table uses the majority of the three runs.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"5 Table 6\",\"text_quote\":\"Unclear 2 Year 9\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Page text row mixes the Articles and Projects panels; 'Unclear 2' is the Articles panel value, 'Year 9' the date-precision panel value.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"This resulted in five relevant articles, eight unclear and 21 not relevant.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Human and LLM relevance coding comparable in categories\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Category sets and mapping to the 2x2 table are not documented.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Report the full LLM category distribution on the pilot (including 'unclear'), the rule used to map to the 2x2 table, and how ties across runs were resolved.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-009\",\"category\":\"data_flow_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The 34-article validation set was used to revise and re-run the prompt before serving as the accuracy benchmark, yet the manuscript says the LLM is 'evaluated against labels it has not seen'. The report does not say whether the 97 percent agreement comes from the first or the revised prompt, or whether the final run used the revised version.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":6,\"page_label\":\"6\",\"section\":\"3.2 LLM pipeline\",\"text_quote\":\"After updating the prompt, the analysis of the validation set of articles\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"None of the human coding was included in the LLM prompt. The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 3.2 says the first-run output was reviewed, the prompt was changed (more complete geography, wider infrastructure types), and 'the analysis of the validation set of articles was repeated'. Human labels were not placed in the prompt, so the claim about unseen labels is literally supported. But the same 34 articles were used for prompt development and for the headline 97 percent agreement. With only 3 relevant articles and 31 non-relevant, agreement is dominated by true negatives. The pilot's lessons on planned vs actual dates and on relative dates (Section 3.1.4) are not reported as incorporated into the prompt used for the 3,187 run.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 6 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_006.md\",\"page\":6,\"page_label\":\"6\",\"section\":\"3.2\",\"text_quote\":\"After updating the prompt, the analysis of the validation set of articles\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e13eccc23f4c883050d15bcf\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote spans a line break.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4\",\"text_quote\":\"The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Validation set is a clean hold-out for the LLM\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Set used for prompt iteration; prompt version for each reported result not stated.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"State which prompt version generated Tables 3-4 and the 3,187-article run, and whether the validation set was used to tune it. Label the 97 percent as development-set agreement and report prevalence-adjusted agreement if desired.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-010\",\"category\":\"denominator_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"Project-level denominators switch between 43 (Table 6, abstract, conclusion) and 44 (Sections 6.2-6.3) without stating the date precision or the day/month status of the 44th (Stord) project. The 29 'day or month' and the 17 + 2 day-dated counts in Section 6.3 therefore cannot be tied to one project set.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":11,\"page_label\":\"11\",\"section\":\"6.3 Proposed econometric analysis\",\"text_quote\":\"Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Of the 44 projects, 18 have an article reporting an official opening ceremony. Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects without a reported ceremony.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 6 reports 43 projects with Day 19, Month 10, Year 9 and Not stated 5 (sum 43). Section 6.3 uses 44 projects (18 with ceremony + 26 without), and day-dated projects total 17 + 2 = 19, equal to Table 6's Day count for 43 projects. That is only compatible if the Stord project was not day-dated, or if the sets are not comparable. The paper does not give Stord's precision, nor the ceremony coding for the 43 versus 44. The propose model (1) uses four categories (none, year, month, day), while Table 6 uses 'Not stated'.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 11 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_011.md\",\"page\":11,\"page_label\":\"11\",\"section\":\"6.3\",\"text_quote\":\"Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-95b2618a59737e0b1725c4df\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"Table 6\",\"text_quote\":\"Coded by the LLM 3,187 Day 19\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Page-text row interleaves the Articles and Projects panels; 'Day 19' is the date-precision panel.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Day-dated projects in Table 6 vs Section 6.3\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Both give 19 day-dated projects but on 43 versus 44 projects.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Is the day-dated count of 19 in Table 6 (43 projects) the same set as 17 + 2 = 19 in Section 6.3 (44 projects)?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"19\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"projects\",\"sample\":\"43 distinct projects, rounds 2-4\",\"denominator\":\"43 projects\",\"context\":\"Table 6 date-precision panel, Day\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"17 + 2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"projects\",\"sample\":\"44 projects (18 with ceremony, 26 without)\",\"denominator\":\"44 projects\",\"context\":\"Day-dated projects by ceremony status in Section 6.3\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Date precision of the Stord project\",\"Whether the ceremony split uses the same 43-project date coding as Table 6\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State the date precision of the Stord project and use a single project denominator, or label each count with its project set (43 vs 44).\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-011\",\"category\":\"denominator_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The seasonal claim that openings 'cluster before winter and summer holidays' is based on monthly 'share of relevant articles' that are not tabulated, while the text acknowledges the archive extraction has few articles from July-August 2026. Monthly denominators (articles coded) and numerators are not shown.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"5 Results\",\"text_quote\":\"the archive extraction contains few articles from July–August 2026\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"October–December 2025 and May–June 2026 have the highest share of relevant articles ... This indicates that openings cluster before winter and summer holidays.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"No table or figure reports the number of articles coded or relevant per month. The share is by publication month of articles (and 92 relevant articles in total), not of opening dates of projects, and relevant articles may include multiple articles per project. With 92 relevant articles over 13 months and uneven extraction by month, shares in some months rest on very small counts. The inference about opening timing mixes article publication timing with project opening timing.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"5 Results\",\"text_quote\":\"the archive extraction contains few articles from July–August 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Tabulate articles coded and relevant by publication month (and projects by opening month), and qualify the seasonality claim by the monthly article counts.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-012\",\"category\":\"variable_construction_unclear\",\"finding_summary\":\"The Appendix A.3.2 rule 'If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table' contradicts the paper's own example and the Figure 2 colour coding. 'bysykkelstativ' contains 'stativ' (Parking & storage, listed before Infrastructure) but is counted as infrastructure. 'syklende' contains 'sykle' (Proximity, listed before Infrastructure) but is listed under Infrastructure.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions\",\"text_quote\":\"are counted as infrastructure\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing “bysykkel” (city bike), such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 9 order is: bicycle, Proximity, Parking & storage, Leisure, Infrastructure, Other. Parking & storage includes the word part 'stativ' (rack), so 'bysykkelstativ' (city bike station) fits Parking & storage earlier than Infrastructure under the stated rule, yet the text and the blue (Infrastructure) bar in Figure 2 classify it as infrastructure. Likewise Proximity includes 'sykle', which is a substring of 'syklende', but Table 9 lists 'syklende' under Infrastructure and Figure 2 shows it blue. The shares for these types in Table 8 (Infrastructure 13.4%, Parking & storage 10.8%, Proximity 10.7%) depend on this rule. The manuscript concedes the rule is coarse, but the stated priority and the reported assignments differ. The hyphenation 'syk-' / 'lende' in the extracted Table 9 is a line wrap and was not altered.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text (rule and example)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2\",\"text_quote\":\"are counted as infrastructure\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Rule sentence 'given the first type in the table' is two lines above in the same paragraph.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text (Table 9 word parts)\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"Table 9\",\"text_quote\":\"“stativ” (rack)\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 9 read from page text, not the structured table file, per parser guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"figure_3.png / page 16 Figure 2 region\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":\"bysykkelstativ (city bike station) 0.5%\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Colour assignment (blue = Infrastructure for bysykkelstativ and syklende) was read from the page 16 image; the text file gives only labels and shares.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"First-match rule yields infrastructure for bysykkelstativ\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"By the stated order, 'stativ' (Parking & storage) precedes Infrastructure.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"State the actual precedence used in the code, or reorder Table 9 to match it, and document how words containing 'sykle' (e.g. 'syklende') and 'stativ' (e.g. 'bysykkelstativ') were assigned.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-013\",\"category\":\"data_flow_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The stated data gap (January-April 2024) is inconsistent with how Figure 3 and its text describe it. The text says only the 'first quarter of 2024' is missing, and Figure 3 plots a Q2 2024 point even though April 2024 is missing. The treatment of this partial quarter is not explained.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":15,\"page_label\":\"15\",\"section\":\"A.1 Norwegian house listing data\",\"text_quote\":\"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing ... The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"A.1 and the Figure 3 caption give the gap as January to April 2024 (four months), which covers all of Q1 and the first month of Q2. The page 16 text says only Q1 2024 is missing. The page image of Figure 3 shows the series with a single missing quarterly point (Q1 2024) and a Q2 2024 point, which would rest on May-June listings only. The last plotted point is Q4 2026, which can contain only October 2026 given the stated end of data. The 'about 44 percent at the end of the period' therefore rests on a one-month quarter. Both partial quarters could differ in composition or seasonality.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 15 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md\",\"page\":15,\"page_label\":\"15\",\"section\":\"A.1\",\"text_quote\":\"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote spans a line break.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"figure_3.png\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_3.png\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"Figure 3\",\"text_quote\":null,\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-22f18338a427285653860df1\",\"correspondence\":\"visual\",\"verification_note\":\"Inspected the Figure 3 region of page_016.png: one missing quarterly point at Q1 2024, a Q2 2024 point present, last point at Q4 2026. Exact quarter positions inferred from axis ticks; no data labels, so uncertain by about one quarter.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Only Q1 2024 is missing\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"A January-April gap also affects Q2 2024.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"State how partial quarters (Q2 2024, Q4 2026) were handled, or drop them from Figure 3 and the endpoint comparison.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-014\",\"category\":\"variable_construction_unclear\",\"finding_summary\":\"County assignment of the FINN.no listings is not described. Figure 4 reports Akershus, Buskerud, Østfold, Vestfold, Telemark, Troms and Finnmark as separate counties over January 2020-October 2026, but the manuscript gives neither the source of the county variable, nor the boundary vintage, nor per-county listing counts.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"low\",\"location\":{\"page\":17,\"page_label\":\"17\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 4\",\"text_quote\":\"Figure 4 shows the share of listings mentioning cycling by county over the whole period\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Figure 4 shows the share of listings mentioning cycling by county over the whole period ... Cycling is mentioned in 61 percent of the listings in Oslo and 52 percent in Akershus.\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"Appendix A does not document how counties were assigned or what boundary definition was used, and Figure 4 shows no listing counts per county.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"Appendix A.1 describes the dataset period, the exclusion of vacation homes, and the January-April 2024 gap. It does not describe the county variable. Norwegian county boundaries were reorganised on 1 January 2024, splitting several merged counties. The pooled 2020-2026 county shares in Figure 4 may therefore rest on recoded older listings. County shares also pool periods with different overall levels (Figure 3), and the 2024 gap removes the same months for all counties. This is a disclosure gap, not evidence of an error in the computation.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 17 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_017.md\",\"page\":17,\"page_label\":\"17\",\"section\":\"A.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Figure 4 shows the share of listings mentioning cycling by county over the whole period\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e4efa6f7c9c10daa107ce8a0\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Document the county variable (source, boundary vintage, handling of the 2024 reorganisation) and add listing counts per county.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-015\",\"category\":\"variable_construction_unclear\",\"finding_summary\":\"The Table 7 and Section 6.3 variables are only partly defined. Field groups and the 'reported ceremony' attention variable are said to be 'coded by keyword search ... with every match checked by hand', but the keywords are not given and non-matches are not checked, so recall is unknown. Table 7 also takes articles 'flagged by the LLM' as its universe.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":11,\"page_label\":\"11\",\"section\":\"Table 7 note\",\"text_quote\":\"Coded by keyword search for each field group, with every match checked by hand.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Number of projects for which at least one article flagged by the LLM contains the information. Coded by keyword search for each field group, with every match checked by hand.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"The note gives a definition (at least one flagged article contains the information) and a method (keyword search with manual checking of matches). Appendix B refers to a repository but the paper does not list the keywords. Manual checking removes false positives only, so counts such as 'Reasons for delay 4' or 'Metadata and coverage 16' may be undercounts. The 'official opening ceremony' variable used in Section 6.3 (18 of 44) is not among the Table 7 groups, and its coding is not described. Table 7's 'between a third and a half' summary also does not match the table: Project status is 24 of 44 and Concurrent interventions 23 of 44 (more than half), while Reasons for delay is 4 of 44.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 11 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_011.md\",\"page\":11,\"page_label\":\"11\",\"section\":\"Table 7 note\",\"text_quote\":\"Coded by keyword search for each field group, with every match checked by hand.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-95b2618a59737e0b1725c4df\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 7 read from the page text, per parser guidance.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Field-group counts are reliable counts of projects\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Keywords and recall not documented.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"List the keywords per field group and the ceremony definition, state whether non-matches were sampled, and correct the 'between a third and a half' wording.\"},{\"id\":\"SAMPLE-016\",\"category\":\"denominator_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The date-accuracy validation rests on 3 articles, conditional on both coders already calling them relevant, with the pilot coder chosen as the reference even though the human coders disagree on one date. The abstract's 'same opening date for all three' and the full-run '29 dated to day or month' therefore have no corresponding validated denominator.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":8,\"page_label\":\"8\",\"section\":\"4.2 Agreement between human and LLM\",\"text_quote\":\"The LLM gives the same date as the pilot coder in all three.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"For the opening date, we compare the three articles that both the pilot coder and the LLM coded as relevant. The LLM gives the same date as the pilot coder in all three.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 4.1 compares dates only for the three articles both coders coded relevant, and the human coders agree in two of three. In the third, the pilot coder used the official opening and the second coder the school-year start. Using the pilot coder as the reference makes LLM-vs-human agreement 3/3 versus 2/3 between humans. Date precision (day, month, year), the variable used for the 29 day/month projects, is not validated. The pilot articles are mostly in-sample for prompt development (see SAMPLE-009). No sample from the 3,187-article run was checked against human coding; Section 8 acknowledges this as a next step, but the Abstract and Conclusion present the 29 dated projects without that qualification.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 8 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md\",\"page\":8,\"page_label\":\"8\",\"section\":\"4.2\",\"text_quote\":\"The LLM gives the same date as the pilot coder in all three.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Quote spans a line break.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1\",\"text_quote\":\"For the opening date, we compare only the three articles that both coders coded as relevant.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"LLM dating validated\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"n = 3, conditional on relevance agreement, single reference coder, no precision validation.\"}],\"numeric_check\":null,\"suggested_fix\":\"Label the date comparison as n = 3, say that no full-run dates or precision categories were validated, and qualify the abstract and conclusion accordingly.\"}],\"notes\":[\"Parser-quality guidance was followed. The structured table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, and Tables 1-9 were read from the page text. Page images for pages 4 and 16 were inspected for Figure 1, Figure 2 colours and Figure 3.\",\"Arithmetic confirmed with no issue: 266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579. The Table 8 shares (38.1, 13.4, 10.8, 10.7, 9.8, 3.8, 1.0 percent) recompute from the counts. The 34 = 5 + 8 + 21 pilot coding sums. The Table 6 date-precision cells sum to 43 (19 + 10 + 9 + 5). The Section 6.3 counts sum to 44 (18 + 26). The Table 3 and 4 cells and the 97% (33/34) agreement figure are consistent.\",\"Figure 3 point positions were read from axis ticks without data labels, so the Q2 2024 and Q4 2026 positions carry about one quarter of uncertainty. The Figure 2 colour assignments were read visually.\",\"The FINN.no appendix has no assigned or treated panel. No download, login, onboarding or follow-up flow exists, so the flow trace used article, pilot and project stages instead.\"],\"completion\":{\"version\":1,\"state\":\"complete\",\"scope_description\":\"Audit of sample construction, data flow and variable construction in the bicycle-infrastructure-paper parsed artifacts. Covered: the pilot flow (70 hits to 34 articles to relevance codes to openings), the full LLM run (3,187 articles to 92 relevant to 43/44 projects), human-human and human-LLM validation tables, the NVDB linkage example, and the FINN.no listing appendix with its word-classification rules, tables and figures.\",\"checks_completed\":[\"Read the full text of all 18 pages and the parser-quality output, and respected its table and figure warnings\",\"Traced the pilot flow 70 to 34 to 5/3 to 2 against Figure 1, Section 3.1, Table 2 and Tables 3-4\",\"Traced the full-run flow 3,187 to 92 to 43 and 96 to 44 against Table 6, Table 7 and footnote 3\",\"Recomputed the Table 8 counts and shares, the pilot coding sums, and the Table 6 and Section 6.3 project counts\",\"Compared the Table 9 word-classification rule and example with Figure 2 colours and the Table 8 types\",\"Checked the data-gap treatment in Appendix A.1 against Figure 3 and its text\",\"Compared human and LLM coding categories and conditioning samples for relevance and date validation\",\"Checked whether main text and appendices define the Table 7 and Section 6.3 variables\"],\"missing_checks\":[],\"evidence_limitations\":[\"The LLM prompt, coding schema, code and keyword lists are in an external repository and were not available, so the LLM's operative relevance rule and the Table 7 keywords could not be inspected.\",\"Figure 3 values have no data labels, so quarter positions are inferred from the axes.\",\"Structured table CSV/markdown was unsafe per the parser-quality guidance, so tables were read from page text and images.\",\"The county-boundary comment in SAMPLE-014 relies on general background knowledge, not retained evidence, and is flagged low confidence.\"]},\"coverage\":[{\"item_id\":\"assigned_remit\",\"source_object_ids\":[],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Traced sample and variable flow for the pilot, full LLM run, validation, NVDB example and FINN.no appendix. Recomputed the counts and shares, compared the table, figure and text denominators, and checked cross-source human/LLM coding definitions.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Sixteen sample-construction, denominator and variable-definition issues found. All central flow stages were attempted. The Table 8 shares and counts reconciled, and the LLM prompt and keyword lists were unavailable.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"SAMPLE-001\",\"SAMPLE-002\",\"SAMPLE-003\",\"SAMPLE-004\",\"SAMPLE-005\",\"SAMPLE-006\",\"SAMPLE-007\",\"SAMPLE-008\",\"SAMPLE-009\",\"SAMPLE-010\",\"SAMPLE-011\",\"SAMPLE-012\",\"SAMPLE-013\",\"SAMPLE-014\",\"SAMPLE-015\",\"SAMPLE-016\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"claim:table8-counts-shares\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f\"],\"claim\":\"Table 8: 266 625 any-mention and 433 954 no-mention listings; shares 38.1% and 61.9% of 700 579 listings.\",\"check_performed\":\"Summed the counts to 700,579 and recomputed every share from the page-15 text rather than the structured table file.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Counts and shares are consistent to rounding. The multi-type note correctly explains why the type rows exceed the any-mention total (346,827 > 266,625).\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"claim:nvdb-linkage-single-case\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195\"],\"claim\":\"Linking one opening to NVDB shows that articles add an exact opening date that NVDB lacks.\",\"check_performed\":\"Read Section 4.3 and Table 5 on page 9: one Homborsund opening, geometry registered 4 September 2026 versus an opening on 5 October 2026.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The claim is scoped to one linked opening, and the dates are internally consistent. The only small difference, 1,492 + 641 = 2,133 m of road-system ranges against a 2,132 m length, is within a metre and not material. Generalisation beyond one case is not claimed.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"claim:agreement-97pct\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf\"],\"claim\":\"The LLM agrees with the human coder on relevance for 97 percent of articles, the same rate as between two human coders.\",\"check_performed\":\"Recomputed 33/34 from Tables 3 and 4 (read from the page text) and checked the conditioning sample and category mapping.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The arithmetic is correct. The denominators include uncodable truncated articles, the unclear mapping is undocumented, and the validation set was used for prompt iteration.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"SAMPLE-004\",\"SAMPLE-008\",\"SAMPLE-009\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer":"sample_construction_auditor","paper_id":"bicycle-infrastructure-paper","run_status":"ok","summary":"The paper has no assigned/treated panel, but it has a sample flow from search hits to unique articles to relevance codes to openings to projects, plus a FINN.no listing appendix. I traced both. The listing counts and shares in Table 8 are internally consistent: 266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579, and the shares recompute. The main problems are in the pilot and full-run article flow. (1) Figure 1 and Section 3.1.2 divide counts of openings by counts of articles and hits. (2) The pilot has two relevance definitions (5 versus 3 relevant articles). (3) A footnote contradicts Table 3 on how the Stord article was coded. (4) The stated exclusion of truncated-text articles is not applied to the pilot. (5) The full-run construction is undefined: rounds, overlap with the pilot, deduplication and truncation handling, and article versus story units. (6) Human 'unclear' coding is not reconciled with the LLM's categories. (7) The validation set was reused after prompt revision, and date validation covers only three articles. (8) Project denominators switch between 43 and 44. (9) The Table 9 first-match rule contradicts its own example and Figure 2 colours. (10) The treatment of the 2024 data gap in Figure 3 is unclear. Parser quality was respected: the structured table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, and the page text and images were used instead.","findings":[{"id":"SAMPLE-001","category":"denominator_mismatch","finding_summary":"Figure 1 and Section 3.1.2 report '2 of 70 search hits' and '2 of 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)' as concerning an opening that took place. The 2 is a count of distinct openings (projects), not articles or hits, so the numerator and denominator are in different units.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Pilot sample / Figure 1","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 3.1.4 states that five articles were coded relevant and these correspond to two unique openings (four Homborsund, one Stod). Figure 1's last bar is labelled 'Distinct openings that took place' (2), but the caption and text express it as a share of 70 hits and of 34 articles. Under the pilot coder's initial coding, 5 of 34 articles (about 15 percent) concern those two openings. Under the validation recoding, 3 of 34 do. The 6 percent figure therefore mixes projects with articles. The abstract's 'only two actual openings' is correctly phrased in project units.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Figure 1 chart also inspected on page_004.png: bars 70, 34 (49% retained), 5 (15% retained), 2."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"2 of 34 unique articles concern an opening","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"The 2 counts distinct openings; the articles about them number five (or three after recoding)."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Report the final funnel stage in one consistent unit. Give the number of articles reporting an opening (and under which relevance rule), and separately the number of distinct openings. Revise the '6 percent' sentence and the Figure 1 caption accordingly."},{"id":"SAMPLE-002","category":"variable_construction_unclear","finding_summary":"The pilot uses two different definitions of 'relevant'. Figure 1 and Section 3.1.4 count 5 relevant articles. The validation (Tables 3-4, abstract) recodes the two pre-opening Homborsund articles as not relevant and uses 3. The recoding is applied to the human labels after the fact, and the manuscript does not say how the LLM prompt's relevance rule treats pre-opening articles.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4 Manual coding of the pilot","text_quote":"they are therefore coded as not relevant, leaving three relevant articles","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. In the validation (Section 4), they are therefore coded as not relevant, leaving three relevant articles.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Figure 1 ('Coded relevant' = 5, 15% retained) and the 3.1.4 coding result (five relevant, eight unclear, 21 not relevant) use the original rule. Table 3/4 give 3 relevant for the pilot coder. The 5-to-3 change is disclosed, but the rule (an article is relevant only if published after the opening) is introduced as a pilot lesson. Table 1 lists relevance as 'Opening of a new walking and cycling path', with no timing condition. The LLM prompt is not reproduced (Appendix B only points to a repository). The reader cannot tell whether the LLM's 'Relevant' in Table 4 and the 92 articles in Table 6 are defined on the 3-article rule, the 5-article rule, or something else.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"they are therefore coded as not relevant, leaving three relevant articles","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Whitespace/line-wrap tolerant quote."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4","text_quote":"The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Pilot relevant count","source_object_ids":["S1"],"relation":"partial","note":"5 in the funnel versus 3 in validation; the LLM's operative definition is not stated in the paper."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"State the operative relevance rule (including the pre-opening and planned-opening treatment) as used by the human coders and the LLM prompt. Show Figure 1 and Tables 3-4 under the same rule, or label each count with its rule."},{"id":"SAMPLE-003","category":"data_flow_inconsistency","finding_summary":"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was 'coded as not relevant by both human coders'. Section 4.1 and Table 3 say the second coder coded the Stord article as relevant (the only human disagreement).","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses / footnote 3","text_quote":"coded as not relevant by both human coders","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The 44 projects include ... the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 3 shows pilot coder Not relevant / second coder Relevant = 1 article. Section 4.1 identifies it as the Stord municipality / Vestland County pedestrian-crossing article. Table 4 shows the same article is the only pilot-coder vs LLM disagreement, with the LLM (majority) coding it relevant. Footnote 3 therefore misdescribes the second coder's coding. The Stord (Vestland) project is also distinct from the Stod (Steinkjer) opening. Its inclusion in the 44 projects is explained only through the LLM flag, which the footnote does not say.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6","text_quote":"96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote 3 (marker digit attached to 'The'); the sentence about Stord continues on the following lines."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1","text_quote":"The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County over a pedestrian crossing.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Stord coded not relevant by both human coders","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"Table 3 (cell 1 in Pilot not relevant / Second coder relevant) and the 4.1 text show the second coder coded it relevant."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Correct footnote 3 to state who coded the Stord article as relevant (second coder and LLM) and that the pilot coder coded it not relevant. State that its inclusion in the 44 projects rests on the LLM flag."},{"id":"SAMPLE-004","category":"sample_restriction_mismatch","finding_summary":"Section 3.1.1 says duplicates and articles with missing or truncated text are excluded before analysis, but the pilot's 34 unique articles still include four articles with 0-23 words and two further very short ones. These are coded 'unclear' and then folded into 'not relevant' in the agreement tables.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.1 News article base","text_quote":"as well as articles with missing or truncated text, are excluded","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"These duplicates, as well as articles with missing or truncated text, are excluded before the analysis.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 3.1.2 says that in four of the 34 unique articles 'the full text in the archive was missing, with only 0-23 words'. Section 3.1.4 says six of the eight 'unclear' articles had too little text, the four missing-text ones and two very short ones. These articles remain in the 34-article denominator of Tables 3-4, where unclear is set to not relevant (Table 3 note, footnote 1). 6 of the 31 'not relevant' pilot-coder cells are therefore articles that carry no codable content. Whether the same exclusion was applied to the 3,187 full-run articles is not stated.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.1-3.1.2","text_quote":"the full text in the archive was missing, with only 0–23 words","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 4 text (exclusion rule)","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.1","text_quote":"as well as articles with missing or truncated text, are excluded","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"This resulted in five relevant articles, eight unclear and 21 not relevant.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Truncated/missing text articles are excluded","source_object_ids":["S2","S1","S3"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"Four missing-text and two very short articles remain in the 34-article pilot and in the agreement tables."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Reconcile the exclusion rule with the pilot flow. Either report agreement excluding the six uncodable articles, or state that the rule applies only to the full run. Report how many truncated-text articles were dropped from the 3,187."},{"id":"SAMPLE-005","category":"data_flow_inconsistency","finding_summary":"The full-run data flow cannot be reconstructed. 'Rounds 1-4' are never defined. The pilot window (2 Sept-10 Oct 2026) lies inside the 'rounds 2-4' window (Oct 2025-Oct 2026), and the manuscript does not say whether the 34 pilot articles are inside the 3,187. Yet the 96 articles and 44 projects add pilot articles to the 92 and 43.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"high","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses / footnote 3","text_quote":"96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The 96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 5 says the LLM coded 3,187 articles 'from rounds 2-4, published between October 2025 and October 2026'. Table 7 draws on 'rounds 1-4'. The pilot was drawn between 2 September and 10 October 2026, which falls inside that window. The 44 projects are described as the 43 from Section 5 plus Stord, so Homborsund and Stod must already be among the 43 through rounds 2-4 articles, while the pilot articles about them are added separately. Round boundaries, search terms/dates per round, and any overlap or deduplication across rounds and with the pilot are not given, so it is unclear whether any article or project is counted twice. The conclusion and abstract report only 43 projects, while Section 6 uses 44.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6","text_quote":"96 articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 9 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md","page":9,"page_label":"9","section":"5 Results","text_quote":"published between October 2025 and October 2026 in 236 different outlets","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Quote spans a line break in the PDF text."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"96 = 92 + 4 pilot; 44 = 43 + Stord","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"partial","note":"Arithmetic adds up, but the round definitions and the overlap of the pilot with rounds 2-4 are not specified."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Define each round (dates, search terms, retrieval date, whether duplicates across rounds were removed) and state whether the pilot articles are inside or outside the 3,187. Provide a single flow of articles and projects across rounds and the pilot."},{"id":"SAMPLE-006","category":"data_flow_inconsistency","finding_summary":"It is unclear whether the 3,187 coded articles and the 92 relevant articles are deduplicated. Section 3.1.1 says duplicates are excluded, but the authors report that the automatic duplicate check missed a near-identical article, and Section 6.4 says coverage must still be counted after duplicates are removed. 'Articles' and 'distinct stories' also appear to be used interchangeably.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":6,"page_label":"6","section":"3.1.4 / 6.4","text_quote":"the automatic duplicate check missed the near-identical online and print versions of one article (Fanaposten)","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The LLM coded 3,187 articles ... The result was 92 articles reporting an opening and 43 unique projects.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"In the pilot, 36 of 70 hits (about 51 percent) were duplicates, and the automatic deduplication still missed at least one near-duplicate. For the 3,187 articles, the number of retrieved hits, the number of duplicates removed and the deduplication method are not reported. Table 7 counts '16 projects covered by more than one distinct story', while Section 5 says most projects are covered by one or two articles and the 92 articles map to 43 projects (about 2.1 per project). Section 6.4 says 'Coverage should be counted at project level after duplicates are removed'. This suggests that duplicated versions may remain in the 92, so the article-level counts and outlets (50) are not clearly in a consistent unit.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 6 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_006.md","page":6,"page_label":"6","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"the automatic duplicate check missed the near-identical online and print versions of one article (Fanaposten)","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e13eccc23f4c883050d15bcf","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Quote spans a line break."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 12 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_012.md","page":12,"page_label":"12","section":"6.4","text_quote":"Coverage should be counted at project level after duplicates are removed.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-a6c6d31e7be45f25b775aa47","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 11 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_011.md","page":11,"page_label":"11","section":"Table 7 note","text_quote":"covered by more than one distinct story","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-95b2618a59737e0b1725c4df","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 7 note, footnote letter 'a' precedes 'Projects'."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Duplicates excluded before analysis","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"partial","note":"No full-run deduplication counts; evidence suggests duplicates may remain."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Report, for the full run, hits retrieved, duplicates and truncated-text articles removed, and the method. State whether the 92 relevant articles are unique stories or include duplicate versions."},{"id":"SAMPLE-007","category":"data_flow_inconsistency","finding_summary":"The selection of the 70 pilot search hits is not documented. The text gives a date window and one search term, but not how the 70 were drawn from the archive, the total number of hits in the window, or whether they are consecutive, random or top-ranked.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Pilot sample","text_quote":"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026 was extracted","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026 was extracted to test our approach.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 3.1.1 reports preliminary counts of 530 to 13,800 hits over three years depending on the term. The pilot yield (3 relevant of 34, about 9 percent) is used to argue that keyword search is too noisy, and the abstract generalises from it. The 3,187-article full run yields 92/3,187 (about 2.9 percent). Without the sampling rule the pilot yield cannot be interpreted, and the sample's representativeness for the full run cannot be judged.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"State how the 70 hits were selected from the archive and how many hits the search returned in the window."},{"id":"SAMPLE-008","category":"variable_construction_unclear","finding_summary":"Human three-way relevance coding (relevant/no/unclear) and LLM coding are not reconciled. Humans coded 8 of 34 pilot articles 'unclear', while the LLM full run reports only 2 'unclear' of 3,187. The paper does not say how LLM 'unclear' outputs, or three-run ties across three categories, enter the 2x2 majority-vote Table 4.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":8,"page_label":"8","section":"4.2 / Table 4 note","text_quote":"the table uses the majority of the three runs.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The LLM coded each article three times, and the table uses the majority of the three runs.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 3.1.4: human coding yielded five relevant, eight unclear, 21 not relevant (8/34 = 24 percent unclear). Footnote 1 on page 7 sets human 'unclear' to not relevant. Table 6 (page 10) reports Unclear 2 among 3,187 LLM-coded articles. The manuscript does not state the LLM's categories in the pilot, how many pilot articles were 'unclear' for the LLM, how 'unclear' or split votes were mapped to 2x2, or whether truncated-text and planned-opening articles (which humans coded unclear) were coded relevant, not relevant or unclear by the LLM.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 8 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md","page":8,"page_label":"8","section":"Table 4 note","text_quote":"the table uses the majority of the three runs.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"5 Table 6","text_quote":"Unclear 2 Year 9","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Page text row mixes the Articles and Projects panels; 'Unclear 2' is the Articles panel value, 'Year 9' the date-precision panel value."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"This resulted in five relevant articles, eight unclear and 21 not relevant.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Human and LLM relevance coding comparable in categories","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"partial","note":"Category sets and mapping to the 2x2 table are not documented."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Report the full LLM category distribution on the pilot (including 'unclear'), the rule used to map to the 2x2 table, and how ties across runs were resolved."},{"id":"SAMPLE-009","category":"data_flow_inconsistency","finding_summary":"The 34-article validation set was used to revise and re-run the prompt before serving as the accuracy benchmark, yet the manuscript says the LLM is 'evaluated against labels it has not seen'. The report does not say whether the 97 percent agreement comes from the first or the revised prompt, or whether the final run used the revised version.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":6,"page_label":"6","section":"3.2 LLM pipeline","text_quote":"After updating the prompt, the analysis of the validation set of articles","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"None of the human coding was included in the LLM prompt. The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 3.2 says the first-run output was reviewed, the prompt was changed (more complete geography, wider infrastructure types), and 'the analysis of the validation set of articles was repeated'. Human labels were not placed in the prompt, so the claim about unseen labels is literally supported. But the same 34 articles were used for prompt development and for the headline 97 percent agreement. With only 3 relevant articles and 31 non-relevant, agreement is dominated by true negatives. The pilot's lessons on planned vs actual dates and on relative dates (Section 3.1.4) are not reported as incorporated into the prompt used for the 3,187 run.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 6 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_006.md","page":6,"page_label":"6","section":"3.2","text_quote":"After updating the prompt, the analysis of the validation set of articles","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e13eccc23f4c883050d15bcf","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Quote spans a line break."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4","text_quote":"The LLM is thus evaluated against labels it has not seen.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Validation set is a clean hold-out for the LLM","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"Set used for prompt iteration; prompt version for each reported result not stated."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"State which prompt version generated Tables 3-4 and the 3,187-article run, and whether the validation set was used to tune it. Label the 97 percent as development-set agreement and report prevalence-adjusted agreement if desired."},{"id":"SAMPLE-010","category":"denominator_mismatch","finding_summary":"Project-level denominators switch between 43 (Table 6, abstract, conclusion) and 44 (Sections 6.2-6.3) without stating the date precision or the day/month status of the 44th (Stord) project. The 29 'day or month' and the 17 + 2 day-dated counts in Section 6.3 therefore cannot be tied to one project set.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":11,"page_label":"11","section":"6.3 Proposed econometric analysis","text_quote":"Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Of the 44 projects, 18 have an article reporting an official opening ceremony. Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects without a reported ceremony.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 6 reports 43 projects with Day 19, Month 10, Year 9 and Not stated 5 (sum 43). Section 6.3 uses 44 projects (18 with ceremony + 26 without), and day-dated projects total 17 + 2 = 19, equal to Table 6's Day count for 43 projects. That is only compatible if the Stord project was not day-dated, or if the sets are not comparable. The paper does not give Stord's precision, nor the ceremony coding for the 43 versus 44. The propose model (1) uses four categories (none, year, month, day), while Table 6 uses 'Not stated'.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 11 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_011.md","page":11,"page_label":"11","section":"6.3","text_quote":"Of these, 17 can be dated to the day, compared with 2 of the 26 projects","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-95b2618a59737e0b1725c4df","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"Table 6","text_quote":"Coded by the LLM 3,187 Day 19","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Page-text row interleaves the Articles and Projects panels; 'Day 19' is the date-precision panel."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Day-dated projects in Table 6 vs Section 6.3","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"Both give 19 day-dated projects but on 43 versus 44 projects."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Is the day-dated count of 19 in Table 6 (43 projects) the same set as 17 + 2 = 19 in Section 6.3 (44 projects)?","quantities":[{"value":"19","source_id":"S2","unit":"projects","sample":"43 distinct projects, rounds 2-4","denominator":"43 projects","context":"Table 6 date-precision panel, Day","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"17 + 2","source_id":"S1","unit":"projects","sample":"44 projects (18 with ceremony, 26 without)","denominator":"44 projects","context":"Day-dated projects by ceremony status in Section 6.3","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"missing_information":["Date precision of the Stord project","Whether the ceremony split uses the same 43-project date coding as Table 6"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"State the date precision of the Stord project and use a single project denominator, or label each count with its project set (43 vs 44)."},{"id":"SAMPLE-011","category":"denominator_mismatch","finding_summary":"The seasonal claim that openings 'cluster before winter and summer holidays' is based on monthly 'share of relevant articles' that are not tabulated, while the text acknowledges the archive extraction has few articles from July-August 2026. Monthly denominators (articles coded) and numerators are not shown.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"5 Results","text_quote":"the archive extraction contains few articles from July–August 2026","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"October–December 2025 and May–June 2026 have the highest share of relevant articles ... This indicates that openings cluster before winter and summer holidays.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"No table or figure reports the number of articles coded or relevant per month. The share is by publication month of articles (and 92 relevant articles in total), not of opening dates of projects, and relevant articles may include multiple articles per project. With 92 relevant articles over 13 months and uneven extraction by month, shares in some months rest on very small counts. The inference about opening timing mixes article publication timing with project opening timing.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"5 Results","text_quote":"the archive extraction contains few articles from July–August 2026","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Tabulate articles coded and relevant by publication month (and projects by opening month), and qualify the seasonality claim by the monthly article counts."},{"id":"SAMPLE-012","category":"variable_construction_unclear","finding_summary":"The Appendix A.3.2 rule 'If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table' contradicts the paper's own example and the Figure 2 colour coding. 'bysykkelstativ' contains 'stativ' (Parking & storage, listed before Infrastructure) but is counted as infrastructure. 'syklende' contains 'sykle' (Proximity, listed before Infrastructure) but is listed under Infrastructure.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions","text_quote":"are counted as infrastructure","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing “bysykkel” (city bike), such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 9 order is: bicycle, Proximity, Parking & storage, Leisure, Infrastructure, Other. Parking & storage includes the word part 'stativ' (rack), so 'bysykkelstativ' (city bike station) fits Parking & storage earlier than Infrastructure under the stated rule, yet the text and the blue (Infrastructure) bar in Figure 2 classify it as infrastructure. Likewise Proximity includes 'sykle', which is a substring of 'syklende', but Table 9 lists 'syklende' under Infrastructure and Figure 2 shows it blue. The shares for these types in Table 8 (Infrastructure 13.4%, Parking & storage 10.8%, Proximity 10.7%) depend on this rule. The manuscript concedes the rule is coarse, but the stated priority and the reported assignments differ. The hyphenation 'syk-' / 'lende' in the extracted Table 9 is a line wrap and was not altered.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 18 text (rule and example)","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2","text_quote":"are counted as infrastructure","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Rule sentence 'given the first type in the table' is two lines above in the same paragraph."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 18 text (Table 9 word parts)","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"Table 9","text_quote":"“stativ” (rack)","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 9 read from page text, not the structured table file, per parser guidance."},{"id":"S3","type":"figure","label":"figure_3.png / page 16 Figure 2 region","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"Figure 2","text_quote":"bysykkelstativ (city bike station) 0.5%","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Colour assignment (blue = Infrastructure for bysykkelstativ and syklende) was read from the page 16 image; the text file gives only labels and shares."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"First-match rule yields infrastructure for bysykkelstativ","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"By the stated order, 'stativ' (Parking & storage) precedes Infrastructure."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"State the actual precedence used in the code, or reorder Table 9 to match it, and document how words containing 'sykle' (e.g. 'syklende') and 'stativ' (e.g. 'bysykkelstativ') were assigned."},{"id":"SAMPLE-013","category":"data_flow_inconsistency","finding_summary":"The stated data gap (January-April 2024) is inconsistent with how Figure 3 and its text describe it. The text says only the 'first quarter of 2024' is missing, and Figure 3 plots a Q2 2024 point even though April 2024 is missing. The treatment of this partial quarter is not explained.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":15,"page_label":"15","section":"A.1 Norwegian house listing data","text_quote":"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing ... The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"A.1 and the Figure 3 caption give the gap as January to April 2024 (four months), which covers all of Q1 and the first month of Q2. The page 16 text says only Q1 2024 is missing. The page image of Figure 3 shows the series with a single missing quarterly point (Q1 2024) and a Q2 2024 point, which would rest on May-June listings only. The last plotted point is Q4 2026, which can contain only October 2026 given the stated end of data. The 'about 44 percent at the end of the period' therefore rests on a one-month quarter. Both partial quarters could differ in composition or seasonality.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 15 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md","page":15,"page_label":"15","section":"A.1","text_quote":"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Quote spans a line break."},{"id":"S2","type":"figure","label":"figure_3.png","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_3.png","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"Figure 3","text_quote":null,"url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-22f18338a427285653860df1","correspondence":"visual","verification_note":"Inspected the Figure 3 region of page_016.png: one missing quarterly point at Q1 2024, a Q2 2024 point present, last point at Q4 2026. Exact quarter positions inferred from axis ticks; no data labels, so uncertain by about one quarter."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Only Q1 2024 is missing","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"A January-April gap also affects Q2 2024."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"State how partial quarters (Q2 2024, Q4 2026) were handled, or drop them from Figure 3 and the endpoint comparison."},{"id":"SAMPLE-014","category":"variable_construction_unclear","finding_summary":"County assignment of the FINN.no listings is not described. Figure 4 reports Akershus, Buskerud, Østfold, Vestfold, Telemark, Troms and Finnmark as separate counties over January 2020-October 2026, but the manuscript gives neither the source of the county variable, nor the boundary vintage, nor per-county listing counts.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"low","location":{"page":17,"page_label":"17","section":"A.2 / Figure 4","text_quote":"Figure 4 shows the share of listings mentioning cycling by county over the whole period","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Figure 4 shows the share of listings mentioning cycling by county over the whole period ... Cycling is mentioned in 61 percent of the listings in Oslo and 52 percent in Akershus.","assessment":"cannot_verify","cannot_verify_reason":"Appendix A does not document how counties were assigned or what boundary definition was used, and Figure 4 shows no listing counts per county.","evidence_summary":"Appendix A.1 describes the dataset period, the exclusion of vacation homes, and the January-April 2024 gap. It does not describe the county variable. Norwegian county boundaries were reorganised on 1 January 2024, splitting several merged counties. The pooled 2020-2026 county shares in Figure 4 may therefore rest on recoded older listings. County shares also pool periods with different overall levels (Figure 3), and the 2024 gap removes the same months for all counties. This is a disclosure gap, not evidence of an error in the computation.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 17 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_017.md","page":17,"page_label":"17","section":"A.2","text_quote":"Figure 4 shows the share of listings mentioning cycling by county over the whole period","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e4efa6f7c9c10daa107ce8a0","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Document the county variable (source, boundary vintage, handling of the 2024 reorganisation) and add listing counts per county."},{"id":"SAMPLE-015","category":"variable_construction_unclear","finding_summary":"The Table 7 and Section 6.3 variables are only partly defined. Field groups and the 'reported ceremony' attention variable are said to be 'coded by keyword search ... with every match checked by hand', but the keywords are not given and non-matches are not checked, so recall is unknown. Table 7 also takes articles 'flagged by the LLM' as its universe.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":11,"page_label":"11","section":"Table 7 note","text_quote":"Coded by keyword search for each field group, with every match checked by hand.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Number of projects for which at least one article flagged by the LLM contains the information. Coded by keyword search for each field group, with every match checked by hand.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"The note gives a definition (at least one flagged article contains the information) and a method (keyword search with manual checking of matches). Appendix B refers to a repository but the paper does not list the keywords. Manual checking removes false positives only, so counts such as 'Reasons for delay 4' or 'Metadata and coverage 16' may be undercounts. The 'official opening ceremony' variable used in Section 6.3 (18 of 44) is not among the Table 7 groups, and its coding is not described. Table 7's 'between a third and a half' summary also does not match the table: Project status is 24 of 44 and Concurrent interventions 23 of 44 (more than half), while Reasons for delay is 4 of 44.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 11 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_011.md","page":11,"page_label":"11","section":"Table 7 note","text_quote":"Coded by keyword search for each field group, with every match checked by hand.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-95b2618a59737e0b1725c4df","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 7 read from the page text, per parser guidance."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Field-group counts are reliable counts of projects","source_object_ids":["S1"],"relation":"partial","note":"Keywords and recall not documented."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"List the keywords per field group and the ceremony definition, state whether non-matches were sampled, and correct the 'between a third and a half' wording."},{"id":"SAMPLE-016","category":"denominator_mismatch","finding_summary":"The date-accuracy validation rests on 3 articles, conditional on both coders already calling them relevant, with the pilot coder chosen as the reference even though the human coders disagree on one date. The abstract's 'same opening date for all three' and the full-run '29 dated to day or month' therefore have no corresponding validated denominator.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":8,"page_label":"8","section":"4.2 Agreement between human and LLM","text_quote":"The LLM gives the same date as the pilot coder in all three.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"For the opening date, we compare the three articles that both the pilot coder and the LLM coded as relevant. The LLM gives the same date as the pilot coder in all three.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 4.1 compares dates only for the three articles both coders coded relevant, and the human coders agree in two of three. In the third, the pilot coder used the official opening and the second coder the school-year start. Using the pilot coder as the reference makes LLM-vs-human agreement 3/3 versus 2/3 between humans. Date precision (day, month, year), the variable used for the 29 day/month projects, is not validated. The pilot articles are mostly in-sample for prompt development (see SAMPLE-009). No sample from the 3,187-article run was checked against human coding; Section 8 acknowledges this as a next step, but the Abstract and Conclusion present the 29 dated projects without that qualification.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 8 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md","page":8,"page_label":"8","section":"4.2","text_quote":"The LLM gives the same date as the pilot coder in all three.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Quote spans a line break."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1","text_quote":"For the opening date, we compare only the three articles that both coders coded as relevant.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"LLM dating validated","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"n = 3, conditional on relevance agreement, single reference coder, no precision validation."}],"numeric_check":null,"suggested_fix":"Label the date comparison as n = 3, say that no full-run dates or precision categories were validated, and qualify the abstract and conclusion accordingly."}],"notes":["Parser-quality guidance was followed. The structured table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, and Tables 1-9 were read from the page text. Page images for pages 4 and 16 were inspected for Figure 1, Figure 2 colours and Figure 3.","Arithmetic confirmed with no issue: 266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579. The Table 8 shares (38.1, 13.4, 10.8, 10.7, 9.8, 3.8, 1.0 percent) recompute from the counts. The 34 = 5 + 8 + 21 pilot coding sums. The Table 6 date-precision cells sum to 43 (19 + 10 + 9 + 5). The Section 6.3 counts sum to 44 (18 + 26). The Table 3 and 4 cells and the 97% (33/34) agreement figure are consistent.","Figure 3 point positions were read from axis ticks without data labels, so the Q2 2024 and Q4 2026 positions carry about one quarter of uncertainty. The Figure 2 colour assignments were read visually.","The FINN.no appendix has no assigned or treated panel. No download, login, onboarding or follow-up flow exists, so the flow trace used article, pilot and project stages instead."],"completion":{"version":1,"state":"complete","scope_description":"Audit of sample construction, data flow and variable construction in the bicycle-infrastructure-paper parsed artifacts. Covered: the pilot flow (70 hits to 34 articles to relevance codes to openings), the full LLM run (3,187 articles to 92 relevant to 43/44 projects), human-human and human-LLM validation tables, the NVDB linkage example, and the FINN.no listing appendix with its word-classification rules, tables and figures.","checks_completed":["Read the full text of all 18 pages and the parser-quality output, and respected its table and figure warnings","Traced the pilot flow 70 to 34 to 5/3 to 2 against Figure 1, Section 3.1, Table 2 and Tables 3-4","Traced the full-run flow 3,187 to 92 to 43 and 96 to 44 against Table 6, Table 7 and footnote 3","Recomputed the Table 8 counts and shares, the pilot coding sums, and the Table 6 and Section 6.3 project counts","Compared the Table 9 word-classification rule and example with Figure 2 colours and the Table 8 types","Checked the data-gap treatment in Appendix A.1 against Figure 3 and its text","Compared human and LLM coding categories and conditioning samples for relevance and date validation","Checked whether main text and appendices define the Table 7 and Section 6.3 variables"],"missing_checks":[],"evidence_limitations":["The LLM prompt, coding schema, code and keyword lists are in an external repository and were not available, so the LLM's operative relevance rule and the Table 7 keywords could not be inspected.","Figure 3 values have no data labels, so quarter positions are inferred from the axes.","Structured table CSV/markdown was unsafe per the parser-quality guidance, so tables were read from page text and images.","The county-boundary comment in SAMPLE-014 relies on general background knowledge, not retained evidence, and is flagged low confidence."]},"coverage":[{"item_id":"assigned_remit","source_object_ids":[],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Traced sample and variable flow for the pilot, full LLM run, validation, NVDB example and FINN.no appendix. Recomputed the counts and shares, compared the table, figure and text denominators, and checked cross-source human/LLM coding definitions.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Sixteen sample-construction, denominator and variable-definition issues found. All central flow stages were attempted. The Table 8 shares and counts reconciled, and the LLM prompt and keyword lists were unavailable.","finding_ids":["SAMPLE-001","SAMPLE-002","SAMPLE-003","SAMPLE-004","SAMPLE-005","SAMPLE-006","SAMPLE-007","SAMPLE-008","SAMPLE-009","SAMPLE-010","SAMPLE-011","SAMPLE-012","SAMPLE-013","SAMPLE-014","SAMPLE-015","SAMPLE-016"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"claim:table8-counts-shares","source_object_ids":["OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f"],"claim":"Table 8: 266 625 any-mention and 433 954 no-mention listings; shares 38.1% and 61.9% of 700 579 listings.","check_performed":"Summed the counts to 700,579 and recomputed every share from the page-15 text rather than the structured table file.","status":"checked_no_issue","reason":"Counts and shares are consistent to rounding. The multi-type note correctly explains why the type rows exceed the any-mention total (346,827 > 266,625).","finding_ids":[],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"claim:nvdb-linkage-single-case","source_object_ids":["OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195"],"claim":"Linking one opening to NVDB shows that articles add an exact opening date that NVDB lacks.","check_performed":"Read Section 4.3 and Table 5 on page 9: one Homborsund opening, geometry registered 4 September 2026 versus an opening on 5 October 2026.","status":"checked_no_issue","reason":"The claim is scoped to one linked opening, and the dates are internally consistent. The only small difference, 1,492 + 641 = 2,133 m of road-system ranges against a 2,132 m length, is within a metre and not material. Generalisation beyond one case is not claimed.","finding_ids":[],"attempted":true,"importance":"peripheral","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"claim:agreement-97pct","source_object_ids":["OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf"],"claim":"The LLM agrees with the human coder on relevance for 97 percent of articles, the same rate as between two human coders.","check_performed":"Recomputed 33/34 from Tables 3 and 4 (read from the page text) and checked the conditioning sample and category mapping.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"The arithmetic is correct. The denominators include uncodable truncated articles, the unclear mapping is undocumented, and the validation set was used for prompt iteration.","finding_ids":["SAMPLE-004","SAMPLE-008","SAMPLE-009"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"}]},"ttft_ms":2108,"type":"result","duration_ms":293297,"uuid":"5d775864-d5b4-4ec1-8d1f-d2dd9d7cadd0","ttft_stream_ms":1377,"time_to_request_ms":146,"first_content_frame_ms":1377,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-08T17:18:28.888Z"}
